{
  "id": "28650_dassuru",
  "headword": "{脱|だっ}する",
  "reading": "だっする",
  "romaji": "dassuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to escape from; to break out of; to get out of",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to escape from; to break out of; to extricate oneself from",
      "explanation": "To get free of a difficult situation, state, or place. The thing one escapes is marked with から or, more commonly in this formal register, を. Often used about crises, hardships, or constraining categories."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28650_dassuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{危機|きき}を{脱|だっ}した。",
      "english": "We escaped the crisis.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28650_dassuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{病院|びょういん}で{命|いのち}の{危険|きけん}を{脱|だっ}した。",
      "english": "At the hospital he got out of life-threatening danger.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28650_dassuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{経済|けいざい}はようやく{不況|ふきょう}を{脱|だっ}しつつある。",
      "english": "The economy is finally breaking out of the recession.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive. The state escaped is marked with を: Xを{脱|だっ}する.\n- {脱|だっ}する is a formal, written-register verb. In conversation, から{抜|ぬ}け{出|だ}す or から{逃|に}げる are more typical.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {危機|きき}を{脱|だっ}する: to escape danger\n- {不況|ふきょう}を{脱|だっ}する: to climb out of recession\n- {貧困|ひんこん}を{脱|だっ}する: to escape poverty\n- {素人|しろうと}の{域|いき}を{脱|だっ}する: to move beyond the amateur level\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {抜|ぬ}け{出|だ}す: to slip out; to break free — concrete, everyday register\n- {脱出|だっしゅつ}する: to escape — physical or dramatic escape from a place\n- {免|まぬが}れる: to be spared; to avoid — about avoiding rather than escaping a state already in",
